  Warnings:
  - Whole Building mode requested 458 primary pieces. Large buildings should use
    activation and visible-fragment budgets so all baked Rigidbodies do not wake
    in one frame.
  - Whole Building stitched 1 near-matching modular seam edge(s) within 0,03 source
    units so fracture pieces can cross authored segment boundaries.
  - 'Shell breakdown (triangles, volume, watertight): #1 12 tri, vol 525,027, OPEN;
    #2 4 tri, vol 587,593, OPEN'
  - "Source has 2 separate mesh shells (0 closed, 2 found before preparation). Per-shell
    fracture: OFF (shells fracture merged) \u2014 classified as one hollow shell
    (an inner surface faces inward)."
  - Kept 4 nested surface islands together as one hollow shell. Auto Axis and every
    fracture plane are shared by the outer and inner walls so generated caps connect
    them instead of closing the cavity separately.
  - Concrete fracture safely exported 456 of the configured maximum of 458. The remaining
    candidates would create an open boundary, an extreme needle or an invalid micro-fragment
    merge, so they were not exported.
  - 27 cut segment(s) could not be chained within the normal weld tolerance; affected
    caps preserved their real edge order and closed the final numerical seam.
  - Intact collision uses 2 compound convex parts because the source contains disconnected
    mesh islands.
  - Dense destruction uses stable per-fragment Box Colliders instead of PhysX convex
    cooking. This avoids deferred QuickHull failures when many complex fragments
    activate at once.
  - 'Large Whole Building defers inactive fragment physics: only pieces that actually
    detach receive a Rigidbody. This keeps a local first break from registering all
    456 pieces with PhysX.'
